{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966806,"nonce":"ABo+PB0eWx6xj1NLh5N2mjJOzzM=","title":"Bumping one package's git pin without its inter-package pins builds two copies of a shared","message":"The `/packages/blinc_*` crates git-pin EACH OTHER (not just `Blinc.git`). Bump one package's rev and every OTHER package that pins it must be bumped to match, or cargo links TWO copies of the shared crate and the demo fails with `E0599 no method` / `E0308 mismatched types` (e.g. a `blinc_portal_ui::ButtonBuilder` from rev A doesn't satisfy the trait imported from rev B).\n\n**The root `[patch]` for package URLs is GONE** (as of 2026-07). The workspace root `Cargo.toml` `[patch.\"…Blinc.git\"]` only redirects the CORE crates (blinc_core/layout/gpu/animation/theme/svg/platform) to local `crates/*`. There is NO `[patch]` for `blinc_portal_ui.git` / `blinc_canvas_kit.git` / `blinc_node_editor.git` / `blinc_game_kit.git`, so packages resolve from their pinned git revs on LOCAL builds too. The diamond therefore breaks `cargo build` locally, not only CI. (A dependency's OWN `[patch]` — e.g. node_editor's `portal_ui = ../blinc_portal_ui` — is ignored by cargo; only workspace-root patches apply.)\n\n**The full inter-package pin DAG (bump in leaf-first order, re-push each, then repin the manifests):**\n- `blinc_canvas_kit` — leaf (no package pins). Bump Blinc.git only.\n- `blinc_portal_ui` — pins `canvas_kit`. Bump canvas_kit + Blinc.git.\n- `blinc_game_kit` — pins `canvas_kit`. Bump canvas_kit + Blinc.git.\n- `blinc_node_editor` — pins `canvas_kit` AND `portal_ui`. Bump both + Blinc.git.\n- Consumers: `examples/blinc_app_examples/Cargo.toml` (4 pins) AND `tools/build-web-examples/src/main.rs` (4 hardcoded pins, lines ~147/218/227/235) — repin all 4 to the final consistent HEADs.\n\n**Gotchas that hid the fix:**\n- `Cargo.lock` AND `examples/_generated/` are BOTH gitignored. The lock skew (`grep -A2 'name = \"blinc_portal_ui\"' Cargo.lock` showing \u003e1 `rev=`) is local-only, never committed. After repinning, run `cargo metadata --format-version 1 \u003e/dev/null` to collapse the lock; verify one `rev=` per package.\n- The generated web wrapper crates in `examples/_generated/*/Cargo.toml` carry their own copies of the package pins. Regenerate them with `cargo run -p blinc-build-web-examples -- --no-gallery` (no `--build` = no wasm) AFTER bumping `tools/build-web-examples/src/main.rs`, or their stale pins keep a second package version alive in the lock.\n- Resolve FULL 40-char SHAs before pinning. Watch for a second-order `cargo fmt --check` failure once compilation succeeds.\n\nSee feedback resolve full sha before pinning, feedback explicit push only.","files":null}]}